This infographic on **Digital Literacy** highlights four key areas. First, it defines digital literacy as the ability to find, evaluate, create, and communicate information using technology—combining technical skills with critical thinking and ethics. Second, it recommends useful digital tools for students, such as Google Workspace (Docs, Drive) for collaboration and Zotero/Mendeley for research. Third, it emphasizes staying safe online through strong passwords, privacy settings, and scam awareness. Finally, it explains the importance of building a professional online presence via LinkedIn and portfolios to showcase skills and personal brand.
